# Plan: Prevent Duplicate Fragment Title for Cloned Cards in M@S Studio

## Summary
When a user clones a card in M@S Studio, the clone dialog pre-displays the original fragment's title but the internal `titleClone` state starts empty, so confirming without editing leaves the copy with the same title. This plan adds a `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` method to `MasRepository` that appends an incrementing `-N` suffix when a title collision is detected against the in-memory fragment list, and wires `showClone()` to initialize `titleClone` with the computed unique title before the dialog opens.

## Task Description
- Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle)` to `MasRepository` that:
  - Reads existing titles from `Store.fragments.list.data` (path-scoped to current view)
  - If `baseTitle` is already taken, strips any trailing `-N` suffix to get a root, then returns the first `root-N` not present
- Fix `showClone()` in `MasFragmentEditor` to call the new method and store the result in `this.titleClone`
- Update the clone dialog template to bind `value` to `this.titleClone` instead of `this.fragment.title`
- Reset `titleClone` to `''` in `cancelClone()`
- Add unit tests for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`

## Relevant Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `studio/src/mas-repository.js` | Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle)` method |
| `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` | Modify `showClone()`, clone dialog template, `cancelClone()` |
| `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` | Add unit tests for the new method |

## Step by Step Tasks

### 1. Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` to `MasRepository`

In `studio/src/mas-repository.js`, add the following method to the `MasRepository` class (e.g., right before `copyFragment`):

```js
/**
 * Returns a unique fragment title by appending a numeric suffix if a fragment
 * with the same title already exists in the current in-memory list.
 * Uniqueness is scoped to the currently-loaded tag path (whatever is in Store.fragments.list.data).
 *
 * Examples:
 *   'lucy-card'   (exists) → 'lucy-card-1'
 *   'lucy-card-1' (exists, 'lucy-card' also exists) → 'lucy-card-2'
 *
 * @param {string} baseTitle - The desired title (typically the title of the fragment being cloned)
 * @returns {string} A title guaranteed not to collide with any title in the in-memory list
 */
generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle) {
    const existingTitles = new Set(
        (Store.fragments.list.data.get() || [])
            .map((store) => store.get()?.title)
            .filter(Boolean),
    );

    if (!existingTitles.has(baseTitle)) return baseTitle;

    // Strip trailing -N suffix to get the root title
    const suffixMatch = baseTitle.match(/^(.*)-(\d+)$/);
    const rootTitle = suffixMatch ? suffixMatch[1] : baseTitle;

    let n = 1;
    while (existingTitles.has(`${rootTitle}-${n}`)) {
        n += 1;
    }
    return `${rootTitle}-${n}`;
}
```

### 2. Initialize `titleClone` with a unique title in `showClone()`

In `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`, update `showClone()`:

**Before:**
```js
async showClone() {
    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {
        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();
        if (!confirmed) return;
    }
    this.showCloneDialog = true;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);
}
```

**After:**
```js
async showClone() {
    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {
        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();
        if (!confirmed) return;
    }
    this.titleClone = this.repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle(this.fragment.title);
    this.showCloneDialog = true;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);
}
```

### 3. Bind clone dialog title input to `this.titleClone`

In `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`, update the `cloneConfirmationDialog` getter template — change the `sp-textfield` `value` binding:

**Before:**
```js
value="${this.fragment.title}"
```

**After:**
```js
value="${this.titleClone}"
```

### 4. Reset `titleClone` in `cancelClone()`

In `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`, update `cancelClone()`:

**Before:**
```js
cancelClone() {
    this.showCloneDialog = false;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(false);
    this.tagsClone = [];
    this.osiClone = null;
}
```

**After:**
```js
cancelClone() {
    this.showCloneDialog = false;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(false);
    this.tagsClone = [];
    this.osiClone = null;
    this.titleClone = '';
}
```

### 5. Add unit tests in `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`

Add a new `describe` block for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`:

```js
describe('MasRepository#generateUniqueFragmentTitle', () => {
    let sandbox;
    let repository;

    beforeEach(() => {
        sandbox = sinon.createSandbox();
        repository = Object.create(MasRepository.prototype);
    });

    afterEach(() => {
        sandbox.restore();
        Store.fragments.list.data.set([]);
    });

    function makeStore(title) {
        return { get: () => ({ title }) };
    }

    it('returns the base title unchanged when no collision exists', () => {
        Store.fragments.list.data.set([makeStore('other-card')]);
        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card')).to.equal('lucy-card');
    });

    it('appends -1 when the base title already exists', () => {
        Store.fragments.list.data.set([makeStore('lucy-card')]);
        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card')).to.equal('lucy-card-1');
    });

    it('increments suffix beyond -1 when -1 also exists', () => {
        Store.fragments.list.data.set([makeStore('lucy-card'), makeStore('lucy-card-1')]);
        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card')).to.equal('lucy-card-2');
    });

    it('strips existing suffix and increments when cloning a -N card', () => {
        Store.fragments.list.data.set([makeStore('lucy-card'), makeStore('lucy-card-1')]);
        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card-1')).to.equal('lucy-card-2');
    });

    it('handles an empty fragment list gracefully', () => {
        Store.fragments.list.data.set([]);
        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('my-card')).to.equal('my-card');
    });
});
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Cloning a card whose Fragment Title already exists in the current path produces a clone titled `<base>-1`
- [ ] If `<base>-1` also exists, the clone is titled `<base>-2`, and so on
- [ ] Cloning a card named `<base>-N` generates `<base>-(N+1)` (or the next available suffix)
- [ ] Cloning a card whose Fragment Title is unique returns the title unchanged (no suffix added)
- [ ] The original card's Fragment Title is not modified
- [ ] Manual edits in the clone dialog are not blocked — the user may change the pre-filled title freely
- [ ] `cancelClone()` resets `titleClone` to `''` so stale values don't persist on re-open

## Validation Commands

- `node --check studio/src/mas-repository.js`
- `node --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`
- `node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`

